  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 304 AM EDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nYet another mainly quiet early morning in the north woods. No\nprecip in the region. Stratus and fog have been slowly expanding,\nmainly in the north half of our area (Straits area and north). \nDRM/MCD/SJX/SLH are all seeing occasionally dense fog. The same \nis probably oozing into western Mackinac Co, and MQT does have a\nfog advisory bordering us this morning.\n\nSeveral more hours for fog to further expand, though to this\npoint that expansion has been slow. Still on the fence as to\nwhether an advisory will be needed here. Fog and lower clouds\nwill gradually erode this morning. Otherwise uneventful this\nafternoon/evening, before more fog returns later tonight,\nespecially ne lower MI.\n\nCurrent western US 500mb trof progressing inland, will\neventually leave behind a cutoff low over the desert SW. The\nnorthern portion of this remains more progressive, deepening as\nit eventually moves toward Hudson Bay by early Sunday. In\nadvance of these features, ridging gets pumped up into the Great\nLakes. Slightly warmer temps are thus progged for Friday and\nSaturday. That ridge starts to get suppressed beginning Sat\nnight, but some of the models do not lower heights in our area \nas much as they did at this time yesterday. Instead the ridge \nonly gets substantially flattened, at least in some guidance. \nThe ECMWF is a less troffy, less chilly solution for next week \ncompared to the GFS.\n\nThe passing system to our north will still promote a chance for\nshowers in eastern upper MI, centered on Sunday morning. Still\ncooler for next week. 50s for highs in northern lower MI,\nperhaps some upper 40s in eastern upper, Monday and beyond. Some\nslight chances for mostly rain showers are progged early to mid\nweek, as overall model spread remains somewhat high.",
